# Permission gate render order (glob-scoped)

Operator incident (2026-08-15): twenty-nine admin SPA pages evaluated
`canView` before `useEffectivePermissionsState().resolved`, flashing a false
"you do not have permission" Alert while the IAM session was still loading.
An empty permission set is indistinguishable from denied until settled.

Glob-scoped only — not always-apply.

## The rule

> **While IAM permissions are unresolved, render a loading state — never
> granted content and never a permission denial. Only after `resolved` is
> true may the page show a real denial or the protected body. Defaulting to
> permissive rendering while unresolved would be a security-floor regression
> under `baseline-security-perfect-always.mdc`. Enforced by
> `ui/scripts/audit-permission-gate.mjs` in `prebuild` and `lint` with
> `--deny`.**

## Required pattern

```tsx
const { permissions: perms, resolved } = useEffectivePermissionsState()
const canView = hasAnyRequiredPermission(perms, …)

if (!resolved) return <PermissionsLoading label="…" />
if (!canView) return <Alert>…real denial…</Alert>
```

OT pages may use `useOtPermissions()` + `OtPermissionsLoading`. Hiding with
`if (!resolved || !canView) return null` is safe (no denial chrome).

Reference: `ui/src/auth/PermissionsLoading.tsx`, `PermissionGate.tsx`,
commit `c7a41f1f2`.

## Forbidden

- `if (!canView) return <Alert>…` before any `!resolved` loading gate.
- `useEffectivePermissions()` on a page that renders permission denial UI
  (use `useEffectivePermissionsState()` instead).
- Removing `audit:permission-gate` from `prebuild` / `lint` or dropping
  `--deny` to make a build pass.

Deferred gaps are listed in `ui/docs/permission-gate-deferred.md` until the
sibling agent lands fixes; remove rows as files go green.

